2026-11-20 21:26 Design questions (built with the conservative default, open for the maintainer):
Q1 bind: NOT built. rke2 bind-address would move the apiserver off 127.0.0.1:6443, which Rex::Rancher's Cilium (k8sServiceHost 127.0.0.1:6443 on rke2) and the server's own components use; Rex::Rancher::Server::install_server has no bind/advertise option either. Default: the firewall closes 6443/9345 on the public IP (Hetzner firewalls default-deny inbound and act on the public interface only); advertise/etcd move to the private IP through node-ip. Wanted? Needs a lab check and a rex-rancher ticket (option for bind-address/advertise-address, or a host-level drop rule).
Q2 Primary IPs: not assigned. Servers get a fresh auto-delete Primary IP from Hetzner; the existing ones stay untouched. Reusing them needs a mapping primary IP -> server (one per CP? per pool node?) -- which? Note WWW::Hetzner create drops ipv4=>id unless enable_ipv4/public_net is passed too.
Q3 no public IPv4 at all (egress via the edge NAT): not built, public IPv4 kept.
Q4 shape: per-entry keys network/firewalls/address (+ tls_san on control planes), not a cluster-level switch; address: private needs network. Riding on the OCPNode spec, not OCPNodeProvider (per-type CR, shared by all pools).
Q5 reconcile path: under address: private OCP reads control_planes[].private_ip where it read public_ip; nothing writes either back after the first apply (the operator pins it). Also found: Config::cluster_status says 'hetzner pins public_ip in the spec', but no code writes it.
Q6 ocp node add has no --network/--firewall/--address; a hand-added node gets them only via its spec.

